Notes on things not fully implemented / simplifications:

- **Captive turning hostile:** the spec's two contradictory behaviors are resolved as "shooting a formation boss destroys the captive with it" (explosion, no return); the captive never becomes a separately flying hostile — it only fires while riding with its diving boss.
- **Tractor beam vs dual fighter:** the beam only captures a single fighter; a dual fighter is immune to capture (it can still be shot apart). In the real arcade one dual half could be captured.
- **Score-table colors / title screen art** are approximations (no exact arcade font or logo); flags are drawn as numbered red pennants (stage 1 shows a plain "1" marker).
- **Entry-path shapes and dive curves** are original bezier curves in the spirit of the arcade (specific choreography per stage is not reproduced exactly).
- The stage-start jingle is an original arpeggio, not the copyrighted arcade tune.
- Entry-group dives and a few arcade edge cases (e.g., boss re-capture while a captive already exists, escorts during beam dives) are omitted by design; bosses only beam when no fighter is currently captive.
